        "original_id": "1d351397-f983-596c-97ac-466c78d782db",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thomas Parker Sanborn, Franklin Benjamin Sanborn, George Santayana\n- Works: The Last Puritan\n- Topics: abolitionism, social science, American transcendentalism, national identity\n\nFacts:\n- Franklin Benjamin Sanborn was an abolitionist, a social scientist, and a memorialist of American transcendentalism.\n- Thomas Parker Sanborn was the eldest son of Franklin Benjamin Sanborn.\n- George Santayana was originally from Spain.\n- George Santayana was raised and educated in the United States from the age of eight.\n- George Santayana identified himself as an American, although he always kept a valid Spanish passport.\n- Thomas Parker Sanborn became a close friend of George Santayana.\n- Thomas Parker Sanborn was a model for the protagonist in George Santayana's only novel, The Last Puritan.",
